WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:17.194
Mandy walked through the agora.

2
00:00:17.214 --> 00:00:20.176
"How could they just leave me!"

3
00:00:20.897 --> 00:00:21.497
she thought.

4
00:00:21.517 --> 00:00:26.220
"It seems boys get to do anything they want here.

5
00:00:27.001 --> 00:00:28.101
But girls don't!"

6
00:00:29.522 --> 00:00:31.604
She wandered around the marketplace.

7
00:00:33.212 --> 00:00:35.654
It was hot and she was getting tired.

8
00:00:35.674 --> 00:00:40.017
"I hope Vinnie comes back soon," she thought.

9
00:00:42.378 --> 00:00:45.881
Finally she stopped to wait in front of a small house.

10
00:00:47.241 --> 00:00:50.103
She noticed some sheep's wool pinned to the door.

11
00:00:50.123 --> 00:00:53.986
"That's odd," she said to herself.

12
00:00:54.006 --> 00:00:59.750
"Ah, you have a new baby sister," a voice said from behind her.

13
00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.952
Mandy turned to look at the speaker.

14
00:01:04.012 --> 00:01:06.854
He was a short man in a long white robe.

15
00:01:07.794 --> 00:01:09.495
He had a full white beard.

16
00:01:09.515 --> 00:01:12.497
"I beg your pardon?"

17
00:01:13.317 --> 00:01:14.097
Mandy said.

18
00:01:14.978 --> 00:01:20.041
Pointing to the wool, the man said, "That means a new baby girl.

19
00:01:21.141 --> 00:01:24.323
For a boy, your family would hang olive leaves."

20
00:01:25.243 --> 00:01:28.745
"Why do they hang wool?

21
00:01:29.246 --> 00:01:30.286
Or olive leaves?

22
00:01:30.706 --> 00:01:31.987
Or anything at all?"

23
00:01:32.687 --> 00:01:33.488
Mandy asked.

24
00:01:34.688 --> 00:01:37.871
"Everyone in the city knows this," said the man.

25
00:01:37.891 --> 00:01:40.233
"Yet you question it.

26
00:01:40.713 --> 00:01:44.656
Why?" Mandy looked the man right in the eye.

27
00:01:44.676 --> 00:01:49.600
"Because I don't understand," she replied.

28
00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:53.823
"Ah! You seek understanding," he said.

29
00:01:55.825 --> 00:01:57.206
Three men walked up.

30
00:01:57.647 --> 00:01:58.847
They seemed excited.

31
00:01:58.867 --> 00:02:04.332
"Great Socrates," said one of the men, "your students are waiting."

32
00:02:06.776 --> 00:02:08.597
Mandy's mouth dropped open.

33
00:02:13.479 --> 00:02:14.239
she stuttered.

34
00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:18.321
"He is one of the greatest teachers of all time!"

35
00:02:18.961 --> 00:02:20.182
she said to herself.

36
00:02:21.282 --> 00:02:23.263
Socrates smiled at Mandy.

37
00:02:24.103 --> 00:02:26.624
"Let's walk to the Parthenon," he said.

38
00:02:27.925 --> 00:02:31.907
Meanwhile, back at the gymnasium, Vinnie looked around.

39
00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.788
The gymnasium was huge!

40
00:02:35.444 --> 00:02:37.466
He saw some young men wrestling.

41
00:02:38.746 --> 00:02:40.908
Others threw a ball back and forth.

42
00:02:42.309 --> 00:02:45.911
A musician played a lyre while a group of boys listened.

43
00:02:47.152 --> 00:02:50.695
Jason wrapped long strips of leather around his knuckles.

44
00:02:51.575 --> 00:02:53.176
He was getting ready to box.

45
00:02:53.196 --> 00:02:55.998
"Vinnie, come train with us!"

46
00:02:56.679 --> 00:02:57.299
he cried.

47
00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:01.062
"No, thanks," Vinnie said shyly.

48
00:03:01.082 --> 00:03:04.084
"Come on," said Jason.

49
00:03:04.856 --> 00:03:06.677
"Boxing will make you strong!"

50
00:03:06.697 --> 00:03:08.837
"Oh really?"

51
00:03:09.597 --> 00:03:10.798
a voice boomed.

52
00:03:11.598 --> 00:03:13.418
"Everyone knows wrestling is better!"

53
00:03:13.438 --> 00:03:16.779
"Not again," said Jason.

54
00:03:16.799 --> 00:03:18.500
"It's Milo."

55
00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.781
Milo showed them a thick rope.

56
00:03:23.341 --> 00:03:25.021
He tied it around his head.

57
00:03:25.041 --> 00:03:26.742
"Watch this!"

58
00:03:27.442 --> 00:03:28.262
said Milo.

59
00:03:28.282 --> 00:03:31.543
"You are about to see an amazing feat of strength!"

60
00:03:32.644 --> 00:03:35.744
"Don't show off," groaned Jason.

61
00:03:36.765 --> 00:03:39.025
Milo took a deep breath and held it.

62
00:03:40.166 --> 00:03:41.966
His face turned very red.

63
00:03:42.566 --> 00:03:44.407
He held his breath even longer.

64
00:03:45.447 --> 00:03:47.407
The veins in his forehead swelled.

65
00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.768
His head looked like it might explode.

66
00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:53.289
Everyone watched closely.

67
00:03:54.369 --> 00:03:56.270
Pop! The rope broke!

68
00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.811
All the boys shouted and clapped.
